  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\n### Interpretation\nThe deadline for filing the annual income tax return is a fixed date, which is April 15. This applies to all individual taxpayers, including those who are self-employed and professionals. If April 15 falls on a weekend or holiday, the deadline may be extended to the next business day.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers should ensure that their income tax returns are prepared and submitted by this deadline to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. It is advisable to start gathering necessary documents and information well in advance of the deadline to facilitate timely filing.",
